---
// The data-deletion page (also the URL for Play Console's data deletion question).
import ProseLayout from "../layouts/ProseLayout.astro";
import { app, contactEmail } from "../config";
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Delete your data"
  description={`How to delete what ${app.name} keeps, on your phone and on its server.`}
>
  <p>
    {app.name} has no accounts. Almost everything it stores is on your phone.
    The only thing kept on {app.name}'s server is an anonymous ID for your phone
    and the cloud AI minutes it used, and only if you've used cloud AI.
  </p>

  <h2>Delete your cloud data</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open {app.name} and go to <strong>Settings → Cloud AI</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tap <strong>Delete my cloud data</strong>, then confirm.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    {app.name}'s server forgets this phone's anonymous ID and the minutes it
    used. Nothing else is kept there, and your projects aren't affected. If you
    use cloud AI again later, the phone gets a new ID.
  </p>

  <h2>Delete what's on your phone</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A project:</strong> delete it in {app.name}; its files go with it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Working copies:</strong>
      <strong>Settings → Clear preview cache</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Crash reports:</strong>{" "}
      <strong>Settings → Crash reports → Delete</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Everything:</strong> uninstall {app.name}. That removes everything
      it stored on your phone, except videos, GIFs, audio and photos you
      exported to your gallery.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you can't open the app</h2>
  <p>
    The anonymous ID isn't linked to your name, email or phone number, so we
    can't find a phone's data from an email alone. It's deleted automatically
    after 13 months without use. If you need help, email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> and we'll do what we
    can.
  </p>
  <p>
    More about what {app.name} does with data:{" "}
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
